# Shared Types

## Single Source of Truth

- **All shared types live in `backend/src/shared/`**: Modules must not define their own copies of API or domain types
- **Export via `shared/index.ts`**: Other code imports from `../shared` or `@/shared`, not deep paths like `../shared/types/api`
- **Prefer interfaces** for API contracts and shared entities; use type aliases for unions/utility types

## Documentation

- **JSDoc for non-obvious types**: Document purpose and constraints for types that are part of the public API or used across modules

## Example

```typescript
// In shared/types/api.ts — single source for API shape
/** Request body for the generate-PRD endpoint. */
export interface GeneratePRDRequest {
  repoId: string;
  input: string;
}

// Other modules import from shared
import type { GeneratePRDRequest, ApiError } from '../../shared';
```
